 "notes": "Names printed without a suffix are written with 'Street' (KOEBEL, PATTERSON, FLOYD, ROVER, LIVINGSTON, NAEHER, DENMAN, FAULKNER); KINDEL is printed without a suffix and is recorded as Kindel Avenue (same key either way). No street is printed with an old name in brackets. Binding gutter: the left page ends at x~1060 on this half (fold shadow); McLean, Floyd, Western at Bank and Division lie on the left page. Overlap with 22-10L (picked on both halves): the McLean column (Bank, Alley (Bank to Dayton block), Dayton W, Fern Alley, Exeter, York, Findlay, Poplar, Sherman, Liberty), Floyd/Bank, Alley/Floyd, Floyd/Dayton W, Fern Alley/Alley (Floyd continuation), that alley/Exeter, Western at Bank, Dayton W, Dayton, Exeter and Naeher, Division/Bank, Holt/Bank, Turner Street/Bank, Turner Alley/Bank, Turner Alley/Holt Alley, Holt/Dayton, the Alley (Findlay to Poplar, east of McLean) at Findlay, Kelly Place and Poplar, and the Dalton column (Findlay, Kelly Place, Poplar, Rover, Sherman, Liberty). McLean's west side is off the left edge here; McLean points are its centre taken from 22-10L (x shift ~-4700 to -4715). Western Avenue centre is midway between building lines (track slightly NE of centre). York jogs at Western (west part 'York Street', Western-Freeman part 'York Street (east of Western)'); York, Findlay and Poplar also jog at Freeman ('... (east of Freeman)'). Bright Alley is in three pieces: BRIGHT Bank-Garden (x~4578), an alley printed only ALLEY Dayton-Naeher (x~4570, recorded as unnamed), and BRIGHT Naeher-York (x~4540). Kline: KLINE AL. Findlay-Poplar (x~3082), S. KLINE ALLEY Poplar-Sherman (x~3650), KLINE ALLEY Sherman-Liberty (leans from x~4185 at Sherman to ~4207 at Liberty). The N-S alley Findlay-Poplar at x~5188 is printed only ALLEY (Kent Alley in 1904); it is collinear with WOLF'S alley south of Poplar, so the Poplar point is entered for both. Wolf Alley (WOLF ... ALLEY) is the diagonal from Poplar to Wolf's Alley. Kelly Alley (KELLY ... ALLEY) runs from Western to that N-S alley; Kelly Place (PLACE) runs east of Dalton from the 10 ft N-S alley near McLean (x~558) to Kline Alley. Rover west of Dalton is printed ROVER (22-10L); east of Dalton the same alley line is printed only ALLEY and is recorded as Rover Street to South Kline Alley. Floyd: see 22-10L notes (its centreline meets Bank's inside the McLean/Bank crossing). Corn Alley, York St., Findlay St., Livingston and Poplar east of Freeman are stubs ending at the edge of the mapping. Faulkner is 42'."
}
